{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790963588,"nonce":"LVOx341UjnTQVGgIMhx9LsmtV8o=","title":"A generic abstract over a scalar loses its type argument and is lowered as i64","message":"Row: Issue4649.\n\n`Val\u003cFloat\u003e` is interned as `Abstract{underlying: None, type_args: [Float]}`\n(tast/ast_lowering/types/mod.rs). ir/mir/types.rs `convert_type` redirects underlying-None to the\ndeclared `Val\u003cT\u003e`, which has no type args, so `substitute_abstract_type_arg` fails and T becomes\nI64. `static var s:Val\u003cFloat\u003e = 10.5; s.incr()` (inline `this++`) adds 1 to the f64 bits\n(prints 10.500000000000002); a local `w:Val\u003cFloat\u003e = 2.5; w.incr()` prints 3.","files":null}]}